    "variable": "next_n",
    "missing_conjunct": "next_n <= INT_MAX",
    "criterion": "Before get_num() narrows the parsed decimal accumulator into the caller-provided int, the parsed precision value next_n must fit in INT_MAX; otherwise the format parser must reject the specifier instead of materializing a negative precision.",
    "description": "The vulnerable parser accepts a decimal precision that fits in mrb_int but not in int, so the later cast creates a negative precision state instead of rejecting the malformed format specifier."
  },
